{"id":"279166945","kind":"article","title":"间隔效应","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":[],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"间隔重复 & 注意力管理","date":"2020-11-08","updated":"2026-10-27","votes":21,"comment_count":8,"minutes":3,"chars":1209,"keywords":["间隔效应","间隔重复","记忆稳定性","稳定化函数","可提取性","SuperMemo"],"summary":"文章解释间隔效应，并区分增加学习间隔可能带来的正面收益与复习过频可能使效果被忽略的负面解释。作者以记忆的双组分模型和稳定化函数统一二者，称每条记忆痕迹都有使预期效果最大化的复习时机；SuperMemo 数据显示，稳定性较低、内容较复杂的记忆可能有更明显的间隔效应。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/279166945","restoration":null,"toc":[],"html":"<p data-pid=\"So0pF10B\">间隔效应是指在较长的时间间隔后成功回忆的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">记忆增长</a>幅度更大。</p><p data-pid=\"noqLdOhT\"><b>间隔效应可以借助<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization_curve\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定化曲线</a>来精确表达，该曲线将该效应定义为<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">记忆稳定化</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>随时间的增长。详见：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization_curve\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定化曲线</a></b></p><p data-pid=\"jGDS9zCv\">间隔效应有积极和消极的解释，产生一定程度的困惑：</p><ul><li data-pid=\"KzFl-LbN\">对长间隔的积极解释（又称<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定化</a>）：如果我们在学习中增加间隔（在一定程度上），就能提高学习效果（即间隔效应是有帮助的）。</li><li data-pid=\"2g0CXkuY\">对短间隔的负面解释：如果我们复习的频率过高，复习的结果会被记忆系统忽略（即间隔效应是有害的）。</li></ul><p data-pid=\"KYNNZZ1q\">在<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Two_component_model_of_memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">记忆的双组分模型</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>中，我们使用了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization_function\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定化函数</a>，它解决了上述困惑，指出每个单独的记忆痕迹都有一个最佳的复习时间，这个复习时间可以使预期的记忆效果最大化，这是<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定化</a>和遗<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Forgetting_curve\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">忘概率</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>合成的结果。</p><p data-pid=\"DJKMvsGQ\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/SuperMemo\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SuperMemo</a> 使<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Memory_stabilization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">记忆稳定化</a>最大化成为可能。</p><p data-pid=\"hu7atwRn\">由 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/SuperMemo\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SuperMemo</a> 中<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization_curve\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定化曲线</a>的近似值得出的数据表明，增益随着稳定性的提高而明显下降，随着<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Difficulty\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">难度</a>的提高而略有增加。换句话说，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Robert_Bjork\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Bjork</a> 的老格言是成立的：越难越好。</p><p data-pid=\"ZcqaXqIr\"><b><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性</a>低的记忆和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Complexity\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">复杂的记忆</a>表现出更明显的间隔效应</b></p><p data-pid=\"xrbwUQ4I\">对于那些不太在意知识长期<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Retention\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">保留</a>的人来说，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/SuperMemo\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SuperMemo</a> 也可以说是<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Spaced_learning_favors_survival_of_neurons\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">提高脑力</a>的工具。</p><p data-pid=\"lPAaqsXT\">也可以看看：</p><ul><li data-pid=\"-gAi6ozI\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization_curve\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定化曲线</a></li><li data-pid=\"6D_q4NQa\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Structural_and_molecular_mechanisms_of_the_spacing_effect\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔效应的结构和分子机理</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup></li></ul><figure data-size=\"normal\"><img class=\"origin_image zh-lightbox-thumb\" data-original-token=\"v2-e1ede2a5b017d12f1fa4e01e90bc8f37\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://pic2.zhimg.com/v2-f7bf09bf83738a6203c7df4fe12c182b_r.jpg\" width=\"500\"/></figure><p data-pid=\"agWBAIk9\">图：用 SuperMemo 计算的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization_curve\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定化曲线</a>。水平线显示的是时间，用<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Memory_retrievability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">记忆可提取性</a>表示。竖线显示<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定化</a>，即以<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Memory_stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">记忆稳定性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup>的增长来表示记忆持久性的增加。蓝色圆圈表示在给定的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Retrievability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">可提取性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup>水平下，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性</a>随着<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Review\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">复习</a>的进行而增加多少。蓝色圆圈的大小取决于收集到的数据点的数量。该图由进行 31,721次<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Repetition\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">重复</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-8\"><a href=\"#ref-8\">[8]</a></sup>的 SuperMemo 中的数据产生，其中<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Difficulty\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">难度</a>=0.53，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性</a>=26[天]。<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性增长</a>从<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Retrievability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">可提取性</a>=100% 时的 1.36（SIncMin=1.36）增加到 R=0% 时的 26.31（SIncMax=26.31）。SuperMemo 中 R=90% 时的最佳复习产生 1.86 的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性增长</a>(Stab90 相当于旧 SuperMemos 中的 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/O-Factor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">O-Factor</a>)。表示间隔效应的增益常数等于 2.96，即相对较高，因为符合低<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性</a>分位数。这个数据集的稳定度可以用公式（黄线）精确计算： <img alt=\"26e^{-2.96R}\" class=\"math-eq\" eeimg=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://www.zhihu.com/equation?tex=26e%5E%7B-2.96R%7D\"/> ，产生 0.5069 的微小<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Deviation\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">偏差</a>。巩固曲线用紫色显示，并表明<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Forgetting_index\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">遗忘指数</a>是所提出的数据集的一个可信的学习标准。对于 R 接近 100% 时，所呈现的图形的实际<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Stabilization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">稳定性增长</a>是 0.879，因为是用 2074 次测量得到的。这在图片中并不清晰可见，但可以通过 SuperMemo 中的稳定化矩阵导出进行研究。这意味着稳定化曲线公式在接近 100% 和 0% 的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Retrievability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">可提取性</a>的极端情况下可能是不准确的。这可以解释为，没有任何记忆是可以完美提取或可验证地抹去的（见：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/We_never_forget\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">我们永远不会忘记</a>）。</p><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 稳定化 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"595158577\" href=\"#/post/595158577\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 记忆的两个组成成分 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"179076885\" href=\"#/post/179076885\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 记忆的双组分模型 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"579476637\" href=\"#/post/579476637\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 遗忘曲线 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"274352214\" href=\"#/post/274352214\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 间隔效应的结构与分子机理 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"288609114\" href=\"#/post/288609114\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 记忆稳定性 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"559298549\" href=\"#/post/559298549\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-7\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-7\">↩</a> 记忆可提取性 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"559819340\" href=\"#/post/559819340\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-8\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-8\">↩</a> 重复 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"572444486\" href=\"#/post/572444486\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"277483881","title":"记忆的神经统计模型","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":15,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"283017134","title":"间隔重复中的简化与冗余","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":53,"minutes":3,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"595158577","title":"稳定化","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":8,"minutes":7,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"559819340","title":"记忆可提取性","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":8,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"179076885","title":"记忆的两个组成成分|浓缩通俗版","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":75,"minutes":3,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"274352214","title":"遗忘曲线","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":22,"minutes":5,"reason":"被 3 篇回答共同引用 · Piotr Wozniak"},{"id":"1941069300833190267","title":"感知内容的间隔重复","author":"Giacomo Randazzo","votes":62,"minutes":21,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「间隔重复」· Giacomo Randazzo"},{"id":"1907760881749718522","title":"间隔重复记忆系统：已取得长足进步","author":"Domenic Denicola","votes":261,"minutes":12,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「间隔重复」· Domenic Denicola"},{"id":"649655080","title":"解释 FSRS（上篇）：算法描述与运作原理","author":"ClarityInMadness","votes":110,"minutes":6,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「间隔重复」· ClarityInMadness"},{"id":"571700330","title":"条目","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":5,"minutes":1,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「间隔重复」· Piotr Wozniak"}],"rec_answers":[{"id":"2690587187","title":"应试教育给中国带来了什么？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":1644,"minutes":66,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 1644 赞同","evidence":"该标题/关键词及链接随主译文《学校让人沾染上的 100+ 恶习》的摘录带入；只确认标题/关键词提及，没有逐对独立重述此目标译文的观点。"},{"id":"2024783376297596199","title":"如何看待“学生和家长仅仅希望高中不要凌晨五点半就到校，多睡一个小时，就被指责为想搞快乐教育”这句话？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":804,"minutes":82,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 804 赞同","evidence":"逐对核验：回答用该译文的直接脚注锚点指向文章标题或对应的特定术语。"},{"id":"3333217724","title":"学习是一件反人类的事情吗？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":546,"minutes":90,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 546 赞同","evidence":"正文中有明确指向该译文的知乎内链/链接卡，按直接提及记为1级。"},{"id":"2850382253","title":"有哪些典型的学生思维？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":423,"minutes":66,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 423 赞同","evidence":"正文以链接锚点“间隔效应”明确提及该术语/章节，目标译文摘要与此处语境相符。"},{"id":"3265798117","title":"学习到底是快乐的，还是痛苦的?","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":422,"minutes":88,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 422 赞同","evidence":"正文明确链接到目标词条标题。"}]}